window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b284-a44f7ef351afc352.json"]={sha256:"a44f7ef351afc352bf220c1ecd8a7a74d109edecc03d8aa86c00589b5c8faa96",value:{"id":"b284","title":"消波塊製作與安放","titleEn":"Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"把消波構件的材料品質、形狀與安放接觸連成可追溯驗證。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Connect concrete armour material quality, geometry and placed contacts through traceable verification. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-coast","architectureNodes":[["質量與排水體積","Mass and displaced volume"],["自由熱變形尺度","Free thermal movement scale"],["試體強度與構件","Specimen strength versus unit behavior"],["安放密度與孔隙","Placement density and voids"],["磨耗試驗與壽命","Abrasion testing and service life"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-coast","labels":["質量與排水體積","自由熱變形尺度","試體強度與構件","安放密度與孔隙","磨耗試驗與壽命"],"labelsEn":["Mass and displaced volume","Free thermal movement scale","Specimen strength versus unit behavior","Placement density and voids","Abrasion testing and service life"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾質量3000kg、材料密度2400kg/m³，實體V=M/ρ=1.25m³；海水1025kg/m³時有效重為16.86kN，非產品規格。假設質量由3000增10%為3300kg、材料密度不變，實體體積由1.25增為1.375m³，海水中有效重量由16.86094增至18.54703kN；不是不同形狀構件可按質量互換的證明。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume mass3000kg and density2400kg/m³: solid V=1.25m³. In seawater1025kg/m³ effective weight is16.86kN; these are not product specifications. Increasing mass from3000 to3300kg by10% at unchanged density raises solid volume from1.25 to1.375m³ and submerged weight from16.86094 to18.54703kN. This does not justify substituting different unit shapes by mass. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b284-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「質量與排水體積」與「有效用水與配比」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mass and displaced volume\" and \"Effective water accounting\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b284-v15-01","title":"質量與排水體積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mass and displaced volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「質量與排水體積」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mass and displaced volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"混凝土消波構件的質量影響水下有效重量，但水工功能還取決於形狀、接觸和孔隙。從密度換算體積只是一致性檢查，不能由相同噸數推定不同專利形狀的穩定性相同，也不能取代裂縫和缺角檢查。 假設乾質量3000kg、材料密度2400kg/m³，實體V=M/ρ=1.25m³；海水1025kg/m³時有效重為16.86kN，非產品規格。 質量驗證也應保留水下有效重的定義，浸水可達孔隙會影響排水體積。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「質量與排水體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Concrete-unit mass influences submerged weight, while hydraulic behavior also depends on shape, contacts and voids. Density-to-volume conversion is a consistency check, not evidence that different proprietary shapes with equal tonnage have equal stability or freedom from cracking and missing corners. Assume mass3000kg and density2400kg/m³: solid V=1.25m³. In seawater1025kg/m³ effective weight is16.86kN; these are not product specifications. Mass checks must retain the submerged-weight definition because water-accessible voids can affect the displaced volume used for buoyancy calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mass and displaced volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「質量與排水體積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mass and displaced volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-01-k1","title":"質量與排水體積","titleEn":"Mass and displaced volume","text":"混凝土消波構件的質量影響水下有效重量，但水工功能還取決於形狀、接觸和孔隙。從密度換算體積只是一致性檢查，不能由相同噸數推定不同專利形狀的穩定性相同，也不能取代裂縫和缺角檢查。","textEn":"Concrete-unit mass influences submerged weight, while hydraulic behavior also depends on shape, contacts and voids. Density-to-volume conversion is a consistency check, not evidence that different proprietary shapes with equal tonnage have equal stability or freedom from cracking and missing corners.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「質量與排水體積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mass and displaced volume\" is correct?","options":["任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。","混凝土消波構件的質量影響水下有效重量，但水工功能還取決於形狀、接觸和孔隙。","每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches.","Concrete-unit mass influences submerged weight, while hydraulic behavior also depends on shape, contacts and voids.","Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio."],"answer":1,"explanation":"混凝土消波構件的質量影響水下有效重量，但水工功能還取決於形狀、接觸和孔隙。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Concrete-unit mass influences submerged weight, while hydraulic behavior also depends on shape, contacts and voids. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b284-v15-02","title":"質量與排水體積：定量估算","titleEn":"Mass and displaced volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「質量與排水體積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mass and displaced volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾質量3000kg、材料密度2400kg/m³，實體V=M/ρ=1.25m³；海水1025kg/m³時有效重為16.86kN，非產品規格。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume mass3000kg and density2400kg/m³: solid V=1.25m³. In seawater1025kg/m³ effective weight is16.86kN; these are not product specifications. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每一代表構件的秤重、體積和含水狀態對照，查看模具尺寸及外觀紀錄是否相符。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare representative unit weight, volume and moisture state with mould and visual records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾質量3000kg、材料密度2400kg/m³，實體V=M/ρ=1.25m³；海水1025kg/m³時有效重為16.86kN，非產品規格。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume mass3000kg and density2400kg/m³: solid V=1.25m³. In seawater1025kg/m³ effective weight is16.86kN; these are not product specifications.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「質量與排水體積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mass and displaced volume\", which statement holds?","options":["完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。","對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently.","Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b284-v15-03","title":"質量與排水體積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mass and displaced volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「質量與排水體積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mass and displaced volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每一代表構件的秤重、體積和含水狀態對照，查看模具尺寸及外觀紀錄是否相符。另以設計採用的形狀分類檢查接觸，避免僅用質量取代完整幾何驗證。另列缺角位置相對主要接觸臂的位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare representative unit weight, volume and moisture state with mould and visual records. Independently check contact behavior for the specified shape family rather than substituting mass measurement for complete geometric verification. Locate missing corners relative to the primary contact arms. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將每一代表構件的秤重、體積和含水狀態對照，查看模具尺寸及外觀紀錄是否相符。另以設計採用的形狀分類檢查接觸，避免僅用質量取代完整幾何驗證。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare representative unit weight, volume and moisture state with mould and visual records. Independently check contact behavior for the specified shape family rather than substituting mass measurement for complete geometric verification.","failure":"注意干擾：缺角可能只減少少量質量卻破壞主要接觸臂，密度平均值因此仍合格。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A missing corner may remove little mass but destroy an important contact arm while average density still passes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每一代表構件的秤重、體積和含水狀態對照，查看模具尺寸及外觀紀錄是否相符。另以設計採用的形狀分類檢查接觸，避免僅用質量取代完整幾何驗證。另列缺角位置相對主要接觸臂的位置。","textEn":"Compare representative unit weight, volume and moisture state with mould and visual records. Independently check contact behavior for the specified shape family rather than substituting mass measurement for complete geometric verification. Locate missing corners relative to the primary contact arms.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將每一代表構件的秤重、體積和含水狀態對照，查看模具尺寸及外觀紀錄是否相符。另以設計採用的形狀分類檢查接觸，避免僅用質量取代完整幾何驗證。","textEn":"Compare representative unit weight, volume and moisture state with mould and visual records. Independently check contact behavior for the specified shape family rather than substituting mass measurement for complete geometric verification.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「質量與排水體積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mass and displaced volume\"?","options":["將每一代表構件的秤重、體積和含水狀態對照，查看模具尺寸及外觀紀錄是否相符。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。"],"optionsEn":["Compare representative unit weight, volume and moisture state with mould and visual records.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將每一代表構件的秤重、體積和含水狀態對照，查看模具尺寸及外觀紀錄是否相符。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare representative unit weight, volume and moisture state with mould and visual records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b284-v15-04","title":"質量與排水體積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mass and displaced volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「質量與排水體積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mass and displaced volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"缺角可能只減少少量質量卻破壞主要接觸臂，密度平均值因此仍合格。若只按噸數出廠，安放後互鎖下降可能直到暴風才被發現，修復亦更困難。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A missing corner may remove little mass but destroy an important contact arm while average density still passes. Mass-only release can conceal reduced interlock until a storm reveals a defect that is then harder to repair. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：質量驗證也應保留水下有效重的定義，浸水可達孔隙會影響排水體積。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mass checks must retain the submerged-weight definition because water-accessible voids can affect the displaced volume used for buoyancy calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"缺角可能只減少少量質量卻破壞主要接觸臂，密度平均值因此仍合格。若只按噸數出廠，安放後互鎖下降可能直到暴風才被發現，修復亦更困難。","textEn":"A missing corner may remove little mass but destroy an important contact arm while average density still passes. Mass-only release can conceal reduced interlock until a storm reveals a defect that is then harder to repair.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「質量與排水體積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mass and displaced volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","缺角可能只減少少量質量卻破壞主要接觸臂，密度平均值因此仍合格。","每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A missing corner may remove little mass but destroy an important contact arm while average density still passes.","Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio."],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺角可能只減少少量質量卻破壞主要接觸臂，密度平均值因此仍合格。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A missing corner may remove little mass but destroy an important contact arm while average density still passes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b284-v15-05","title":"有效用水與配比：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective water accounting: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「有效用水與配比」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective water accounting” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"配比中的有效用水量要考慮骨材吸水與表面水，不是水表讀值單獨決定。水膠比與工作性、強度和耐久性相關，但本課示意只追蹤收支，不能由一個比值保證大型異形構件內部密實。 假設膠材340kg、加入水170kg，其中8kg被乾骨材吸收且無表面水，有效水膠比(170−8)/340=0.4765；非配方建議。 膠材不一定只有水泥，計算分母需要遵循核准配比中對膠材的明確定義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效用水與配比」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Effective mix water depends on aggregate absorption and surface moisture, not just the metered addition. Water-to-binder ratio relates to workability, strength and durability, but this illustration tracks accounting only; one ratio cannot guarantee consolidation inside a large complex unit. Assume binder340kg and water170kg, with8kg absorbed by dry aggregate and no surface water. Effective ratio=(170−8)/340=0.4765, not a mix recommendation. Binder need not consist only of cement; the calculation denominator must follow the explicit binder definition in the approved mixture. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective water accounting” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效用水與配比」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective water accounting”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-05-k1","title":"有效用水與配比","titleEn":"Effective water accounting","text":"配比中的有效用水量要考慮骨材吸水與表面水，不是水表讀值單獨決定。水膠比與工作性、強度和耐久性相關，但本課示意只追蹤收支，不能由一個比值保證大型異形構件內部密實。","textEn":"Effective mix water depends on aggregate absorption and surface moisture, not just the metered addition. Water-to-binder ratio relates to workability, strength and durability, but this illustration tracks accounting only; one ratio cannot guarantee consolidation inside a large complex unit.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「有效用水與配比」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective water accounting\" is correct?","options":["每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。","整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。","配比中的有效用水量要考慮骨材吸水與表面水，不是水表讀值單獨決定。"],"optionsEn":["Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio.","Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress.","Effective mix water depends on aggregate absorption and surface moisture, not just the metered addition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"配比中的有效用水量要考慮骨材吸水與表面水，不是水表讀值單獨決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Effective mix water depends on aggregate absorption and surface moisture, not just the metered addition. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b284-v15-06","title":"有效用水與配比：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective water accounting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效用水與配比」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective water accounting” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設膠材340kg、加入水170kg，其中8kg被乾骨材吸收且無表面水，有效水膠比(170−8)/340=0.4765；非配方建議。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume binder340kg and water170kg, with8kg absorbed by dry aggregate and no surface water. Effective ratio=(170−8)/340=0.4765, not a mix recommendation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別記錄骨材含水、吸水試驗和加水量，說明哪些水被計入有效水量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record aggregate moisture, absorption testing and added water separately, identifying effective-water assumptions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設膠材340kg、加入水170kg，其中8kg被乾骨材吸收且無表面水，有效水膠比(170−8)/340=0.4765；非配方建議。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume binder340kg and water170kg, with8kg absorbed by dry aggregate and no surface water. Effective ratio=(170−8)/340=0.4765, not a mix recommendation.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「有效用水與配比」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective water accounting\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。","總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms.","Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b284-v15-07","title":"有效用水與配比：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective water accounting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效用水與配比」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective water accounting” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別記錄骨材含水、吸水試驗和加水量，說明哪些水被計入有效水量。核對工作性與代表試體，不以現場臨時加水改善外觀而略過核准配比和追溯紀錄。確認加水與骨材試驗的時間相符。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record aggregate moisture, absorption testing and added water separately, identifying effective-water assumptions. Check workability and representative specimens without treating unrecorded field water addition as an acceptable substitute for the approved mixture. Confirm matching times for water addition and aggregate testing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別記錄骨材含水、吸水試驗和加水量，說明哪些水被計入有效水量。核對工作性與代表試體，不以現場臨時加水改善外觀而略過核准配比和追溯紀錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record aggregate moisture, absorption testing and added water separately, identifying effective-water assumptions. Check workability and representative specimens without treating unrecorded field water addition as an acceptable substitute for the approved mixture.","failure":"注意干擾：骨材含水變化未修正會讓相同水表數字對應不同水膠比，局部泌水或離析也可能出現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uncorrected aggregate moisture gives different effective ratios at identical meter readings and can produce bleeding or segregation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別記錄骨材含水、吸水試驗和加水量，說明哪些水被計入有效水量。核對工作性與代表試體，不以現場臨時加水改善外觀而略過核准配比和追溯紀錄。確認加水與骨材試驗的時間相符。","textEn":"Record aggregate moisture, absorption testing and added water separately, identifying effective-water assumptions. Check workability and representative specimens without treating unrecorded field water addition as an acceptable substitute for the approved mixture. Confirm matching times for water addition and aggregate testing.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別記錄骨材含水、吸水試驗和加水量，說明哪些水被計入有效水量。核對工作性與代表試體，不以現場臨時加水改善外觀而略過核准配比和追溯紀錄。","textEn":"Record aggregate moisture, absorption testing and added water separately, identifying effective-water assumptions. Check workability and representative specimens without treating unrecorded field water addition as an acceptable substitute for the approved mixture.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「有效用水與配比」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective water accounting\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","分別記錄骨材含水、吸水試驗和加水量，說明哪些水被計入有效水量。","外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Record aggregate moisture, absorption testing and added water separately, identifying effective-water assumptions.","Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分別記錄骨材含水、吸水試驗和加水量，說明哪些水被計入有效水量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record aggregate moisture, absorption testing and added water separately, identifying effective-water assumptions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b284-v15-08","title":"有效用水與配比：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective water accounting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效用水與配比」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective water accounting” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"骨材含水變化未修正會讓相同水表數字對應不同水膠比，局部泌水或離析也可能出現。只看試體平均強度，仍可能漏掉構件細長部位的弱區。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uncorrected aggregate moisture gives different effective ratios at identical meter readings and can produce bleeding or segregation. An acceptable average specimen strength may still conceal weak material in slender portions of the actual unit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：膠材不一定只有水泥，計算分母需要遵循核准配比中對膠材的明確定義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Binder need not consist only of cement; the calculation denominator must follow the explicit binder definition in the approved mixture.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"骨材含水變化未修正會讓相同水表數字對應不同水膠比，局部泌水或離析也可能出現。只看試體平均強度，仍可能漏掉構件細長部位的弱區。","textEn":"Uncorrected aggregate moisture gives different effective ratios at identical meter readings and can produce bleeding or segregation. An acceptable average specimen strength may still conceal weak material in slender portions of the actual unit.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「有效用水與配比」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective water accounting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。","骨材含水變化未修正會讓相同水表數字對應不同水膠比，局部泌水或離析也可能出現。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress.","Uncorrected aggregate moisture gives different effective ratios at identical meter readings and can produce bleeding or segregation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"骨材含水變化未修正會讓相同水表數字對應不同水膠比，局部泌水或離析也可能出現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uncorrected aggregate moisture gives different effective ratios at identical meter readings and can produce bleeding or segregation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b284-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「自由熱變形尺度」與「約束冷卻與裂縫」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Free thermal movement scale\" and \"Restrained cooling and cracking\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b284-v15-09","title":"自由熱變形尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Free thermal movement scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「自由熱變形尺度」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Free thermal movement scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大型混凝土構件的表面與內部溫度歷程不同，均勻自由伸縮只能提供基礎量級。若存在溫度梯度或模具約束，就會額外產生應力；把自由變形算式誤當成裂縫預測會遺漏養護和形狀的作用。 假設α=10⁻⁵/K、均勻溫差25K、長L=2m，自由變形ΔL=αΔTL=0.0005m=0.50mm；不含約束。 膨脹係數也可能因骨材而異，模型固定係數不等於所有混凝土都具有相同熱行為。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「自由熱變形尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The surface and core of a large unit follow different temperature histories. Uniform free expansion supplies a basic scale only; gradients or mould restraint generate additional stress. Treating free movement as a crack prediction omits curing conditions and geometric effects. Assumeα=10⁻⁵/K, uniform change25K and length2m. Free movement ΔL=αΔTL=0.0005m=0.50mm, excluding restraint. Thermal expansion depends on aggregate as well, so a fixed coefficient in the example does not imply identical behavior for every concrete. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Free thermal movement scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「自由熱變形尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Free thermal movement scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-09-k1","title":"自由熱變形尺度","titleEn":"Free thermal movement scale","text":"大型混凝土構件的表面與內部溫度歷程不同，均勻自由伸縮只能提供基礎量級。若存在溫度梯度或模具約束，就會額外產生應力；把自由變形算式誤當成裂縫預測會遺漏養護和形狀的作用。","textEn":"The surface and core of a large unit follow different temperature histories. Uniform free expansion supplies a basic scale only; gradients or mould restraint generate additional stress.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自由熱變形尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Free thermal movement scale\" is correct?","options":["大型混凝土構件的表面與內部溫度歷程不同，均勻自由伸縮只能提供基礎量級。","整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。","完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。"],"optionsEn":["The surface and core of a large unit follow different temperature histories.","Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress.","Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大型混凝土構件的表面與內部溫度歷程不同，均勻自由伸縮只能提供基礎量級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The surface and core of a large unit follow different temperature histories. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b284-v15-10","title":"自由熱變形尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Free thermal movement scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「自由熱變形尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Free thermal movement scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設α=10⁻⁵/K、均勻溫差25K、長L=2m，自由變形ΔL=αΔTL=0.0005m=0.50mm；不含約束。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assumeα=10⁻⁵/K, uniform change25K and length2m. Free movement ΔL=αΔTL=0.0005m=0.50mm, excluding restraint. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在厚部與細臂配置相對應的溫度紀錄，區分均勻降溫與內外梯度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare temperature histories in thick portions and slender arms, separating uniform cooling from gradients.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設α=10⁻⁵/K、均勻溫差25K、長L=2m，自由變形ΔL=αΔTL=0.0005m=0.50mm；不含約束。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assumeα=10⁻⁵/K, uniform change25K and length2m. Free movement ΔL=αΔTL=0.0005m=0.50mm, excluding restraint.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「自由熱變形尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Free thermal movement scale\", which statement holds?","options":["對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。"],"optionsEn":["Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b284-v15-11","title":"自由熱變形尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Free thermal movement scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「自由熱變形尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Free thermal movement scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在厚部與細臂配置相對應的溫度紀錄，區分均勻降溫與內外梯度。將實測變形和模具接觸狀態一起比較，確認採用自由膨脹假設的區段是否真的未受拘束。用另一組長度或溫差檢查線性換算。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare temperature histories in thick portions and slender arms, separating uniform cooling from gradients. Relate measured movement to mould contact and verify that portions modeled as freely expanding actually lack significant restraint. Check the linear conversion using another length or temperature interval. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在厚部與細臂配置相對應的溫度紀錄，區分均勻降溫與內外梯度。將實測變形和模具接觸狀態一起比較，確認採用自由膨脹假設的區段是否真的未受拘束。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare temperature histories in thick portions and slender arms, separating uniform cooling from gradients. Relate measured movement to mould contact and verify that portions modeled as freely expanding actually lack significant restraint.","failure":"注意干擾：表面已降溫而核心仍熱時，單一平均溫度會掩蓋內外應變差；局部細臂可能先裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A cooled surface with a warm core creates strain differences hidden by average temperature, potentially cracking slender arms first. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在厚部與細臂配置相對應的溫度紀錄，區分均勻降溫與內外梯度。將實測變形和模具接觸狀態一起比較，確認採用自由膨脹假設的區段是否真的未受拘束。用另一組長度或溫差檢查線性換算。","textEn":"Compare temperature histories in thick portions and slender arms, separating uniform cooling from gradients. Relate measured movement to mould contact and verify that portions modeled as freely expanding actually lack significant restraint. Check the linear conversion using another length or temperature interval.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在厚部與細臂配置相對應的溫度紀錄，區分均勻降溫與內外梯度。將實測變形和模具接觸狀態一起比較，確認採用自由膨脹假設的區段是否真的未受拘束。","textEn":"Compare temperature histories in thick portions and slender arms, separating uniform cooling from gradients. Relate measured movement to mould contact and verify that portions modeled as freely expanding actually lack significant restraint.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「自由熱變形尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Free thermal movement scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。","在厚部與細臂配置相對應的溫度紀錄，區分均勻降溫與內外梯度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage.","Compare temperature histories in thick portions and slender arms, separating uniform cooling from gradients."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在厚部與細臂配置相對應的溫度紀錄，區分均勻降溫與內外梯度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare temperature histories in thick portions and slender arms, separating uniform cooling from gradients. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b284-v15-12","title":"自由熱變形尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Free thermal movement scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「自由熱變形尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Free thermal movement scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面已降溫而核心仍熱時，單一平均溫度會掩蓋內外應變差；局部細臂可能先裂。即使外部總長變化很小，也不能據此排除內部自平衡熱應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A cooled surface with a warm core creates strain differences hidden by average temperature, potentially cracking slender arms first. Small overall length change does not exclude internal self-equilibrating thermal stress within the unit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：膨脹係數也可能因骨材而異，模型固定係數不等於所有混凝土都具有相同熱行為。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Thermal expansion depends on aggregate as well, so a fixed coefficient in the example does not imply identical behavior for every concrete.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面已降溫而核心仍熱時，單一平均溫度會掩蓋內外應變差；局部細臂可能先裂。即使外部總長變化很小，也不能據此排除內部自平衡熱應力。","textEn":"A cooled surface with a warm core creates strain differences hidden by average temperature, potentially cracking slender arms first. Small overall length change does not exclude internal self-equilibrating thermal stress within the unit.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「自由熱變形尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Free thermal movement scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["表面已降溫而核心仍熱時，單一平均溫度會掩蓋內外應變差；局部細臂可能先裂。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。"],"optionsEn":["A cooled surface with a warm core creates strain differences hidden by average temperature, potentially cracking slender arms first.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面已降溫而核心仍熱時，單一平均溫度會掩蓋內外應變差；局部細臂可能先裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A cooled surface with a warm core creates strain differences hidden by average temperature, potentially cracking slender arms first. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b284-v15-13","title":"約束冷卻與裂縫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Restrained cooling and cracking: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「約束冷卻與裂縫」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Restrained cooling and cracking” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"約束會把熱收縮轉換成拉應力，但混凝土齡期、徐變、開裂和約束鬆弛都使反應隨時間變化。完全約束線彈性式只用來比較量級，不能把固定彈性模數一路套到所有養護階段或實際裂縫寬度。 假設E=25GPa、α=10⁻⁵/K、完全約束冷卻25K，σ=EαΔT=6.25MPa拉應力；實際開裂與徐變需另算。 抗拉能力也隨齡期改變，應力和抗力需在相同時間比較才有物理意義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「約束冷卻與裂縫」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Restraint converts thermal contraction into tension, but concrete age, creep, cracking and restraint relaxation change response over time. A fully restrained elastic estimate compares scales only; fixed modulus cannot represent every curing stage or directly predict the resulting crack width. Assume E=25GPa,α=10⁻⁵/K and fully restrained cooling25K. Elastic tensionσ=EαΔT=6.25MPa; cracking and creep require separate treatment. Tensile resistance changes with age too; comparing stress and resistance at the same time is necessary for a physically meaningful interpretation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Restrained cooling and cracking” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「約束冷卻與裂縫」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Restrained cooling and cracking”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-13-k1","title":"約束冷卻與裂縫","titleEn":"Restrained cooling and cracking","text":"約束會把熱收縮轉換成拉應力，但混凝土齡期、徐變、開裂和約束鬆弛都使反應隨時間變化。完全約束線彈性式只用來比較量級，不能把固定彈性模數一路套到所有養護階段或實際裂縫寬度。","textEn":"Restraint converts thermal contraction into tension, but concrete age, creep, cracking and restraint relaxation change response over time. A fully restrained elastic estimate compares scales only; fixed modulus cannot represent every curing stage or directly predict the resulting crack width.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「約束冷卻與裂縫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Restrained cooling and cracking\" is correct?","options":["完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。","約束會把熱收縮轉換成拉應力，但混凝土齡期、徐變、開裂和約束鬆弛都使反應隨時間變化。","抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。"],"optionsEn":["Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently.","Restraint converts thermal contraction into tension, but concrete age, creep, cracking and restraint relaxation change response over time.","Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"約束會把熱收縮轉換成拉應力，但混凝土齡期、徐變、開裂和約束鬆弛都使反應隨時間變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Restraint converts thermal contraction into tension, but concrete age, creep, cracking and restraint relaxation change response over time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b284-v15-14","title":"約束冷卻與裂縫：定量估算","titleEn":"Restrained cooling and cracking: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「約束冷卻與裂縫」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Restrained cooling and cracking” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設E=25GPa、α=10⁻⁵/K、完全約束冷卻25K，σ=EαΔT=6.25MPa拉應力；實際開裂與徐變需另算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume E=25GPa,α=10⁻⁵/K and fully restrained cooling25K. Elastic tensionσ=EαΔT=6.25MPa; cracking and creep require separate treatment. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：記錄溫度、齡期及模具或基座約束，檢查模型採用的彈性模數與實際時間是否一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record temperature, age and mould or base restraint and match modulus to the relevant time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設E=25GPa、α=10⁻⁵/K、完全約束冷卻25K，σ=EαΔT=6.25MPa拉應力；實際開裂與徐變需另算。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume E=25GPa,α=10⁻⁵/K and fully restrained cooling25K. Elastic tensionσ=EαΔT=6.25MPa; cracking and creep require separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「約束冷卻與裂縫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Restrained cooling and cracking\", which statement holds?","options":["總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。","外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area.","Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b284-v15-15","title":"約束冷卻與裂縫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Restrained cooling and cracking: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「約束冷卻與裂縫」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Restrained cooling and cracking” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"記錄溫度、齡期及模具或基座約束，檢查模型採用的彈性模數與實際時間是否一致。用裂縫位置和發展時序比較可能機制，不以一個理想應力直接宣告構件可用。對照開裂時間與材料齡期的強度資料。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record temperature, age and mould or base restraint and match modulus to the relevant time. Compare crack locations and chronology with competing mechanisms rather than declaring a unit acceptable from one ideal elastic stress. Compare cracking time with age-matched material strength evidence. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：記錄溫度、齡期及模具或基座約束，檢查模型採用的彈性模數與實際時間是否一致。用裂縫位置和發展時序比較可能機制，不以一個理想應力直接宣告構件可用。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record temperature, age and mould or base restraint and match modulus to the relevant time. Compare crack locations and chronology with competing mechanisms rather than declaring a unit acceptable from one ideal elastic stress.","failure":"注意干擾：以成熟混凝土模數套用早齡期可能高估或錯排應力時序，忽略徐變又改變鬆弛預測；反之僅因理論值過高而任意刪除約束，也會低估真實裂縫風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using mature modulus at early age can misstate stress magnitude and timing, while omitted creep changes relaxation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"記錄溫度、齡期及模具或基座約束，檢查模型採用的彈性模數與實際時間是否一致。用裂縫位置和發展時序比較可能機制，不以一個理想應力直接宣告構件可用。對照開裂時間與材料齡期的強度資料。","textEn":"Record temperature, age and mould or base restraint and match modulus to the relevant time. Compare crack locations and chronology with competing mechanisms rather than declaring a unit acceptable from one ideal elastic stress. Compare cracking time with age-matched material strength evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"記錄溫度、齡期及模具或基座約束，檢查模型採用的彈性模數與實際時間是否一致。用裂縫位置和發展時序比較可能機制，不以一個理想應力直接宣告構件可用。","textEn":"Record temperature, age and mould or base restraint and match modulus to the relevant time. Compare crack locations and chronology with competing mechanisms rather than declaring a unit acceptable from one ideal elastic stress.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「約束冷卻與裂縫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Restrained cooling and cracking\"?","options":["記錄溫度、齡期及模具或基座約束，檢查模型採用的彈性模數與實際時間是否一致。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Record temperature, age and mould or base restraint and match modulus to the relevant time.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches."],"answer":0,"explanation":"記錄溫度、齡期及模具或基座約束，檢查模型採用的彈性模數與實際時間是否一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record temperature, age and mould or base restraint and match modulus to the relevant time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b284-v15-16","title":"約束冷卻與裂縫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Restrained cooling and cracking: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「約束冷卻與裂縫」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Restrained cooling and cracking” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以成熟混凝土模數套用早齡期可能高估或錯排應力時序，忽略徐變又改變鬆弛預測；反之僅因理論值過高而任意刪除約束，也會低估真實裂縫風險。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using mature modulus at early age can misstate stress magnitude and timing, while omitted creep changes relaxation. Arbitrarily removing restraint merely because the theoretical stress seems high instead understates genuine cracking potential. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：抗拉能力也隨齡期改變，應力和抗力需在相同時間比較才有物理意義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Tensile resistance changes with age too; comparing stress and resistance at the same time is necessary for a physically meaningful interpretation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以成熟混凝土模數套用早齡期可能高估或錯排應力時序，忽略徐變又改變鬆弛預測；反之僅因理論值過高而任意刪除約束，也會低估真實裂縫風險。","textEn":"Using mature modulus at early age can misstate stress magnitude and timing, while omitted creep changes relaxation. Arbitrarily removing restraint merely because the theoretical stress seems high instead understates genuine cracking potential.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「約束冷卻與裂縫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Restrained cooling and cracking\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","以成熟混凝土模數套用早齡期可能高估或錯排應力時序，忽略徐變又改變鬆弛預測；反之僅因理論值過高而任意刪除約束，也會低估真實裂縫風險。","抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using mature modulus at early age can misstate stress magnitude and timing, while omitted creep changes relaxation.","Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以成熟混凝土模數套用早齡期可能高估或錯排應力時序，忽略徐變又改變鬆弛預測；反之僅因理論值過高而任意刪除約束，也會低估真實裂縫風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using mature modulus at early age can misstate stress magnitude and timing, while omitted creep changes relaxation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b284-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「試體強度與構件」與「吊運力向分解」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Specimen strength versus unit behavior\" and \"Resolving handling forces\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b284-v15-17","title":"試體強度與構件：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Specimen strength versus unit behavior: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「試體強度與構件」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Specimen strength versus unit behavior” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"抗壓試體提供特定製作養護和載入條件下的材料證據，異形消波構件卻可能受彎曲、局部接觸和吊運拉力控制。試體與構件的溫度歷程、密實度和尺度不同，因此名義抗壓值不能代表全部構造能力。 假設立方試體邊長0.15m、破壞荷重900kN，f=P/A=900000/0.15²=40MPa；不是直接設計強度。 試體平均值與特徵值的統計意義不同，樣本數及離散程度需另外明列。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「試體強度與構件」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compression specimens provide evidence under specified preparation, curing and loading, while armour units can be governed by bending, local contacts and lifting tension. Their temperature histories, consolidation and size differ, so nominal compressive strength cannot describe every structural capacity of the full unit. Assume a0.15m cube and failure load900kN. f=P/A=900000/0.15²=40MPa is specimen strength, not directly a design strength. A specimen mean and a characteristic value have different statistical meanings, requiring separate statements of sample size and observed variability. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Specimen strength versus unit behavior” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「試體強度與構件」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Specimen strength versus unit behavior”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-17-k1","title":"試體強度與構件","titleEn":"Specimen strength versus unit behavior","text":"抗壓試體提供特定製作養護和載入條件下的材料證據，異形消波構件卻可能受彎曲、局部接觸和吊運拉力控制。試體與構件的溫度歷程、密實度和尺度不同，因此名義抗壓值不能代表全部構造能力。","textEn":"Compression specimens provide evidence under specified preparation, curing and loading, while armour units can be governed by bending, local contacts and lifting tension. Their temperature histories, consolidation and size differ, so nominal compressive strength cannot describe every structural capacity of the full unit.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「試體強度與構件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Specimen strength versus unit behavior\" is correct?","options":["抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。","對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。","抗壓試體提供特定製作養護和載入條件下的材料證據，異形消波構件卻可能受彎曲、局部接觸和吊運拉力控制。"],"optionsEn":["Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms.","Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion.","Compression specimens provide evidence under specified preparation, curing and loading, while armour units can be governed by bending, local contacts and lifting tension."],"answer":2,"explanation":"抗壓試體提供特定製作養護和載入條件下的材料證據，異形消波構件卻可能受彎曲、局部接觸和吊運拉力控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compression specimens provide evidence under specified preparation, curing and loading, while armour units can be governed by bending, local contacts and lifting tension. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b284-v15-18","title":"試體強度與構件：定量估算","titleEn":"Specimen strength versus unit behavior: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「試體強度與構件」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Specimen strength versus unit behavior” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設立方試體邊長0.15m、破壞荷重900kN，f=P/A=900000/0.15²=40MPa；不是直接設計強度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a0.15m cube and failure load900kN. f=P/A=900000/0.15²=40MPa is specimen strength, not directly a design strength. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對試體尺寸、端面、載入方法與養護紀錄，將取樣批次連回實際構件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check specimen dimensions, ends, loading method and curing, linking each sample to its production batch.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設立方試體邊長0.15m、破壞荷重900kN，f=P/A=900000/0.15²=40MPa；不是直接設計強度。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a0.15m cube and failure load900kN. f=P/A=900000/0.15²=40MPa is specimen strength, not directly a design strength.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「試體強度與構件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Specimen strength versus unit behavior\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。","一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts.","Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b284-v15-19","title":"試體強度與構件：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Specimen strength versus unit behavior: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「試體強度與構件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Specimen strength versus unit behavior” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對試體尺寸、端面、載入方法與養護紀錄，將取樣批次連回實際構件。另檢查細臂、轉角與吊點的受力模式，避免讓抗壓試驗代替必要的材料或構造驗證。再檢查試體與構件的養護溫度差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check specimen dimensions, ends, loading method and curing, linking each sample to its production batch. Separately review slender arms, corners and lifting points so compression testing does not replace other necessary material or structural verification. Check curing-temperature differences between specimens and full units. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對試體尺寸、端面、載入方法與養護紀錄，將取樣批次連回實際構件。另檢查細臂、轉角與吊點的受力模式，避免讓抗壓試驗代替必要的材料或構造驗證。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check specimen dimensions, ends, loading method and curing, linking each sample to its production batch. Separately review slender arms, corners and lifting points so compression testing does not replace other necessary material or structural verification.","failure":"注意干擾：試體養護較好時可能高估構件內部品質，局部蜂窩又未必出現在取樣中；平均抗壓值達標仍可能伴隨吊運破裂或安放後接觸臂損傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Better specimen curing can overstate actual unit quality, and sampling may miss local honeycombing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對試體尺寸、端面、載入方法與養護紀錄，將取樣批次連回實際構件。另檢查細臂、轉角與吊點的受力模式，避免讓抗壓試驗代替必要的材料或構造驗證。再檢查試體與構件的養護溫度差異。","textEn":"Check specimen dimensions, ends, loading method and curing, linking each sample to its production batch. Separately review slender arms, corners and lifting points so compression testing does not replace other necessary material or structural verification. Check curing-temperature differences between specimens and full units.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對試體尺寸、端面、載入方法與養護紀錄，將取樣批次連回實際構件。另檢查細臂、轉角與吊點的受力模式，避免讓抗壓試驗代替必要的材料或構造驗證。","textEn":"Check specimen dimensions, ends, loading method and curing, linking each sample to its production batch. Separately review slender arms, corners and lifting points so compression testing does not replace other necessary material or structural verification.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「試體強度與構件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Specimen strength versus unit behavior\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","核對試體尺寸、端面、載入方法與養護紀錄，將取樣批次連回實際構件。","每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check specimen dimensions, ends, loading method and curing, linking each sample to its production batch.","Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對試體尺寸、端面、載入方法與養護紀錄，將取樣批次連回實際構件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check specimen dimensions, ends, loading method and curing, linking each sample to its production batch. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b284-v15-20","title":"試體強度與構件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Specimen strength versus unit behavior: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「試體強度與構件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Specimen strength versus unit behavior” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"試體養護較好時可能高估構件內部品質，局部蜂窩又未必出現在取樣中；平均抗壓值達標仍可能伴隨吊運破裂或安放後接觸臂損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Better specimen curing can overstate actual unit quality, and sampling may miss local honeycombing. A passing mean compressive strength can coexist with lifting fractures or damaged contact arms after placement at the site. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：試體平均值與特徵值的統計意義不同，樣本數及離散程度需另外明列。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A specimen mean and a characteristic value have different statistical meanings, requiring separate statements of sample size and observed variability.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"試體養護較好時可能高估構件內部品質，局部蜂窩又未必出現在取樣中；平均抗壓值達標仍可能伴隨吊運破裂或安放後接觸臂損傷。","textEn":"Better specimen curing can overstate actual unit quality, and sampling may miss local honeycombing. A passing mean compressive strength can coexist with lifting fractures or damaged contact arms after placement at the site.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「試體強度與構件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Specimen strength versus unit behavior\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。","試體養護較好時可能高估構件內部品質，局部蜂窩又未必出現在取樣中；平均抗壓值達標仍可能伴隨吊運破裂或安放後接觸臂損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion.","Better specimen curing can overstate actual unit quality, and sampling may miss local honeycombing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"試體養護較好時可能高估構件內部品質，局部蜂窩又未必出現在取樣中；平均抗壓值達標仍可能伴隨吊運破裂或安放後接觸臂損傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Better specimen curing can overstate actual unit quality, and sampling may miss local honeycombing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b284-v15-21","title":"吊運力向分解：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Resolving handling forces: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「吊運力向分解」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Resolving handling forces” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"消波構件的吊點與重心受複雜形狀影響，索力會因夾角增加而上升。理想兩索靜力分析需同時滿足對稱與共同受力，不能取代專用吊具、動載和早齡期材料能力的核准檢查。 假設質量3000kg、兩索各與垂直45°且靜態對稱，T=3000×9.81/(2cos45°)=20.81kN；未含動載或偏心。 吊點局部作用還取決於嵌件與混凝土的傳力，單一索力不能證明錨定合格。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「吊運力向分解」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Complex geometry affects lifting points and gravity center, and sling force rises with inclination. An ideal two-sling static model requires symmetry and simultaneous engagement; it does not replace approved checks of lifting equipment, dynamics and early-age material capacity. Assume mass3000kg and two symmetric static slings45° from vertical. T=3000×9.81/(2cos45°)=20.81kN, excluding dynamics and eccentricity. Local attachment behavior depends on force transfer through inserts and concrete; one sling-force result cannot establish adequate anchorage performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Resolving handling forces” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「吊運力向分解」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Resolving handling forces”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-21-k1","title":"吊運力向分解","titleEn":"Resolving handling forces","text":"消波構件的吊點與重心受複雜形狀影響，索力會因夾角增加而上升。理想兩索靜力分析需同時滿足對稱與共同受力，不能取代專用吊具、動載和早齡期材料能力的核准檢查。","textEn":"Complex geometry affects lifting points and gravity center, and sling force rises with inclination. An ideal two-sling static model requires symmetry and simultaneous engagement; it does not replace approved checks of lifting equipment, dynamics and early-age material capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「吊運力向分解」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Resolving handling forces\" is correct?","options":["消波構件的吊點與重心受複雜形狀影響，索力會因夾角增加而上升。","對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。","總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Complex geometry affects lifting points and gravity center, and sling force rises with inclination.","Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion.","Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area."],"answer":0,"explanation":"消波構件的吊點與重心受複雜形狀影響，索力會因夾角增加而上升。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Complex geometry affects lifting points and gravity center, and sling force rises with inclination. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b284-v15-22","title":"吊運力向分解：定量估算","titleEn":"Resolving handling forces: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「吊運力向分解」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Resolving handling forces” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設質量3000kg、兩索各與垂直45°且靜態對稱，T=3000×9.81/(2cos45°)=20.81kN；未含動載或偏心。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume mass3000kg and two symmetric static slings45° from vertical. T=3000×9.81/(2cos45°)=20.81kN, excluding dynamics and eccentricity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用實際吊點與重心位置畫自由體圖，核對角度基準、各索受力及局部構件應力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw the actual lifting points and gravity center, checking angle convention, sling forces and local unit stresses.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設質量3000kg、兩索各與垂直45°且靜態對稱，T=3000×9.81/(2cos45°)=20.81kN；未含動載或偏心。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume mass3000kg and two symmetric static slings45° from vertical. T=3000×9.81/(2cos45°)=20.81kN, excluding dynamics and eccentricity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「吊運力向分解」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Resolving handling forces\", which statement holds?","options":["外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b284-v15-23","title":"吊運力向分解：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Resolving handling forces: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「吊運力向分解」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Resolving handling forces” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用實際吊點與重心位置畫自由體圖，核對角度基準、各索受力及局部構件應力。保留核准吊裝方案與材料齡期紀錄，確保教學計算沒有被當作設備操作指令。將吊點能力的證據與索力分開歸檔。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw the actual lifting points and gravity center, checking angle convention, sling forces and local unit stresses. Retain the approved lifting plan and material-age evidence so the teaching calculation is not used as equipment instructions. File attachment-capacity evidence separately from calculated sling forces. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用實際吊點與重心位置畫自由體圖，核對角度基準、各索受力及局部構件應力。保留核准吊裝方案與材料齡期紀錄，確保教學計算沒有被當作設備操作指令。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw the actual lifting points and gravity center, checking angle convention, sling forces and local unit stresses. Retain the approved lifting plan and material-age evidence so the teaching calculation is not used as equipment instructions.","failure":"注意干擾：一索先張緊時對稱分配不成立，構件姿態轉動又會改變吊點力向；早期細臂裂縫可能在後續安放才顯現，僅查總吊重不能追出受損原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Symmetric sharing fails when one sling engages first, while rotation changes attachment force directions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用實際吊點與重心位置畫自由體圖，核對角度基準、各索受力及局部構件應力。保留核准吊裝方案與材料齡期紀錄，確保教學計算沒有被當作設備操作指令。將吊點能力的證據與索力分開歸檔。","textEn":"Draw the actual lifting points and gravity center, checking angle convention, sling forces and local unit stresses. Retain the approved lifting plan and material-age evidence so the teaching calculation is not used as equipment instructions. File attachment-capacity evidence separately from calculated sling forces.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用實際吊點與重心位置畫自由體圖，核對角度基準、各索受力及局部構件應力。保留核准吊裝方案與材料齡期紀錄，確保教學計算沒有被當作設備操作指令。","textEn":"Draw the actual lifting points and gravity center, checking angle convention, sling forces and local unit stresses. Retain the approved lifting plan and material-age evidence so the teaching calculation is not used as equipment instructions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「吊運力向分解」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Resolving handling forces\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。","用實際吊點與重心位置畫自由體圖，核對角度基準、各索受力及局部構件應力。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress.","Draw the actual lifting points and gravity center, checking angle convention, sling forces and local unit stresses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用實際吊點與重心位置畫自由體圖，核對角度基準、各索受力及局部構件應力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw the actual lifting points and gravity center, checking angle convention, sling forces and local unit stresses. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b284-v15-24","title":"吊運力向分解：失效診斷","titleEn":"Resolving handling forces: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「吊運力向分解」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Resolving handling forces” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一索先張緊時對稱分配不成立，構件姿態轉動又會改變吊點力向；早期細臂裂縫可能在後續安放才顯現，僅查總吊重不能追出受損原因。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Symmetric sharing fails when one sling engages first, while rotation changes attachment force directions. Early cracking in slender arms may appear only after placement, and total lifted weight alone cannot explain the damage history. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：吊點局部作用還取決於嵌件與混凝土的傳力，單一索力不能證明錨定合格。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Local attachment behavior depends on force transfer through inserts and concrete; one sling-force result cannot establish adequate anchorage performance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一索先張緊時對稱分配不成立，構件姿態轉動又會改變吊點力向；早期細臂裂縫可能在後續安放才顯現，僅查總吊重不能追出受損原因。","textEn":"Symmetric sharing fails when one sling engages first, while rotation changes attachment force directions. Early cracking in slender arms may appear only after placement, and total lifted weight alone cannot explain the damage history.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吊運力向分解」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Resolving handling forces\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["一索先張緊時對稱分配不成立，構件姿態轉動又會改變吊點力向；早期細臂裂縫可能在後續安放才顯現，僅查總吊重不能追出受損原因。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Symmetric sharing fails when one sling engages first, while rotation changes attachment force directions.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一索先張緊時對稱分配不成立，構件姿態轉動又會改變吊點力向；早期細臂裂縫可能在後續安放才顯現，僅查總吊重不能追出受損原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Symmetric sharing fails when one sling engages first, while rotation changes attachment force directions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b284-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「安放密度與孔隙」與「三維位置與姿態」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Placement density and voids\" and \"Three-dimensional placement geometry\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b284-v15-25","title":"安放密度與孔隙：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Placement density and voids: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「安放密度與孔隙」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Placement density and voids” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"安放密度連結構件數量與覆蓋面積，但互鎖還取決於姿態、層數和接觸位置。每平方米的件數不能直接換成孔隙率，也不能只增加件數就期待水工功能改善，過密可能改變透流與局部架空。 假設同一層200件覆蓋1000m²，安放密度N/A=0.20件/m²；未提供體積與層厚，不能推出孔隙率。 實際斜面和水平面積的選擇會改變名義件數密度，跨專案比較要先統一定義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「安放密度與孔隙」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Placement density relates unit count to area, but interlocking also depends on orientation, layers and contacts. Units per square metre cannot be directly converted into porosity, and adding more units need not improve performance because overly dense placement can alter flow and create unsupported contacts. Assume200 units cover1000m² in one layer. Placement density is0.20units/m²; without volume and thickness it does not determine porosity. Choosing actual slope area versus horizontal projection changes nominal placement density, so comparisons across projects require a consistent denominator first. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Placement density and voids” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「安放密度與孔隙」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Placement density and voids”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-25-k1","title":"安放密度與孔隙","titleEn":"Placement density and voids","text":"安放密度連結構件數量與覆蓋面積，但互鎖還取決於姿態、層數和接觸位置。每平方米的件數不能直接換成孔隙率，也不能只增加件數就期待水工功能改善，過密可能改變透流與局部架空。","textEn":"Placement density relates unit count to area, but interlocking also depends on orientation, layers and contacts. Units per square metre cannot be directly converted into porosity, and adding more units need not improve performance because overly dense placement can alter flow and create unsupported contacts.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「安放密度與孔隙」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Placement density and voids\" is correct?","options":["總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。","安放密度連結構件數量與覆蓋面積，但互鎖還取決於姿態、層數和接觸位置。","構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。"],"optionsEn":["Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area.","Placement density relates unit count to area, but interlocking also depends on orientation, layers and contacts.","Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"安放密度連結構件數量與覆蓋面積，但互鎖還取決於姿態、層數和接觸位置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Placement density relates unit count to area, but interlocking also depends on orientation, layers and contacts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b284-v15-26","title":"安放密度與孔隙：定量估算","titleEn":"Placement density and voids: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「安放密度與孔隙」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Placement density and voids” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設同一層200件覆蓋1000m²，安放密度N/A=0.20件/m²；未提供體積與層厚，不能推出孔隙率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume200 units cover1000m² in one layer. Placement density is0.20units/m²; without volume and thickness it does not determine porosity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明示面積採用水平投影或實際斜面，逐區記錄件數、姿態和接觸照片。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State whether area is horizontal projection or actual slope and record count, orientation and contacts by zone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設同一層200件覆蓋1000m²，安放密度N/A=0.20件/m²；未提供體積與層厚，不能推出孔隙率。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume200 units cover1000m² in one layer. Placement density is0.20units/m²; without volume and thickness it does not determine porosity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「安放密度與孔隙」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Placement density and voids\", which statement holds?","options":["一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。","每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage.","Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b284-v15-27","title":"安放密度與孔隙：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Placement density and voids: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「安放密度與孔隙」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Placement density and voids” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明示面積採用水平投影或實際斜面，逐區記錄件數、姿態和接觸照片。與該構件型式核准的安放規則對照，保留局部空缺而不是用全堤平均密度掩蓋。分別檢查坡腳和坡頂的局部覆蓋。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State whether area is horizontal projection or actual slope and record count, orientation and contacts by zone. Compare the approved rules for that unit type, preserving local gaps rather than hiding them in a whole-structure mean. Check local coverage at toe and crest separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：明示面積採用水平投影或實際斜面，逐區記錄件數、姿態和接觸照片。與該構件型式核准的安放規則對照，保留局部空缺而不是用全堤平均密度掩蓋。","observationEn":"Site practice: State whether area is horizontal projection or actual slope and record count, orientation and contacts by zone. Compare the approved rules for that unit type, preserving local gaps rather than hiding them in a whole-structure mean.","failure":"注意干擾：高處多放構件可以使平均件數達標，坡腳空缺卻仍存在；架空構件在波浪下可能重新轉動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extra units higher up can satisfy average count while toe gaps remain, and bridged units may rotate under waves. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明示面積採用水平投影或實際斜面，逐區記錄件數、姿態和接觸照片。與該構件型式核准的安放規則對照，保留局部空缺而不是用全堤平均密度掩蓋。分別檢查坡腳和坡頂的局部覆蓋。","textEn":"State whether area is horizontal projection or actual slope and record count, orientation and contacts by zone. Compare the approved rules for that unit type, preserving local gaps rather than hiding them in a whole-structure mean. Check local coverage at toe and crest separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"明示面積採用水平投影或實際斜面，逐區記錄件數、姿態和接觸照片。與該構件型式核准的安放規則對照，保留局部空缺而不是用全堤平均密度掩蓋。","textEn":"State whether area is horizontal projection or actual slope and record count, orientation and contacts by zone. Compare the approved rules for that unit type, preserving local gaps rather than hiding them in a whole-structure mean.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「安放密度與孔隙」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Placement density and voids\"?","options":["明示面積採用水平投影或實際斜面，逐區記錄件數、姿態和接觸照片。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。"],"optionsEn":["State whether area is horizontal projection or actual slope and record count, orientation and contacts by zone.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently."],"answer":0,"explanation":"明示面積採用水平投影或實際斜面，逐區記錄件數、姿態和接觸照片。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State whether area is horizontal projection or actual slope and record count, orientation and contacts by zone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b284-v15-28","title":"安放密度與孔隙：失效診斷","titleEn":"Placement density and voids: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「安放密度與孔隙」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Placement density and voids” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高處多放構件可以使平均件數達標，坡腳空缺卻仍存在；架空構件在波浪下可能重新轉動。只驗收總數量，不能確認荷載和互鎖已沿斷面連續傳遞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extra units higher up can satisfy average count while toe gaps remain, and bridged units may rotate under waves. Total quantity alone does not establish continuous contact, load transfer or interlocking along the section. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：實際斜面和水平面積的選擇會改變名義件數密度，跨專案比較要先統一定義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Choosing actual slope area versus horizontal projection changes nominal placement density, so comparisons across projects require a consistent denominator first.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高處多放構件可以使平均件數達標，坡腳空缺卻仍存在；架空構件在波浪下可能重新轉動。只驗收總數量，不能確認荷載和互鎖已沿斷面連續傳遞。","textEn":"Extra units higher up can satisfy average count while toe gaps remain, and bridged units may rotate under waves. Total quantity alone does not establish continuous contact, load transfer or interlocking along the section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「安放密度與孔隙」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Placement density and voids\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","高處多放構件可以使平均件數達標，坡腳空缺卻仍存在；架空構件在波浪下可能重新轉動。","構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Extra units higher up can satisfy average count while toe gaps remain, and bridged units may rotate under waves.","Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高處多放構件可以使平均件數達標，坡腳空缺卻仍存在；架空構件在波浪下可能重新轉動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extra units higher up can satisfy average count while toe gaps remain, and bridged units may rotate under waves. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b284-v15-29","title":"三維位置與姿態：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Three-dimensional placement geometry: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「三維位置與姿態」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Three-dimensional placement geometry” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水下安放需把位置誤差與姿態誤差分開，三維坐標偏差小不代表接觸臂方向正確。測量基準、船體姿態和吊具桿臂都會影響重建位置，圖上的點位必須能追溯到構件的特定參考點。 假設參考點偏差Δx=0.10m、Δy=0.20m、Δz=0.05m，距離e=√(Δx²+Δy²+Δz²)=0.2291m；不是姿態誤差。 位置距離是三維向量的長度，不會保留偏移方向，方向仍需另行記錄。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「三維位置與姿態」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Underwater placement separates position error from orientation error; small coordinate deviation does not establish correct contact-arm direction. Survey datum, vessel attitude and rig lever arms affect reconstruction, so each plotted position must refer to a defined point on the actual unit. Assume reference-point offsets0.10m,0.20m and0.05m. Distance e=√(Δx²+Δy²+Δz²)=0.2291m does not describe orientation error. Position distance is the magnitude of a three-dimensional vector and does not preserve direction, which must therefore remain separately recorded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Three-dimensional placement geometry” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「三維位置與姿態」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Three-dimensional placement geometry”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-29-k1","title":"三維位置與姿態","titleEn":"Three-dimensional placement geometry","text":"水下安放需把位置誤差與姿態誤差分開，三維坐標偏差小不代表接觸臂方向正確。測量基準、船體姿態和吊具桿臂都會影響重建位置，圖上的點位必須能追溯到構件的特定參考點。","textEn":"Underwater placement separates position error from orientation error; small coordinate deviation does not establish correct contact-arm direction. Survey datum, vessel attitude and rig lever arms affect reconstruction, so each plotted position must refer to a defined point on the actual unit.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「三維位置與姿態」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Three-dimensional placement geometry\" is correct?","options":["構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。","外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。","水下安放需把位置誤差與姿態誤差分開，三維坐標偏差小不代表接觸臂方向正確。"],"optionsEn":["Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts.","Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold.","Underwater placement separates position error from orientation error; small coordinate deviation does not establish correct contact-arm direction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水下安放需把位置誤差與姿態誤差分開，三維坐標偏差小不代表接觸臂方向正確。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Underwater placement separates position error from orientation error; small coordinate deviation does not establish correct contact-arm direction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b284-v15-30","title":"三維位置與姿態：定量估算","titleEn":"Three-dimensional placement geometry: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「三維位置與姿態」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Three-dimensional placement geometry” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設參考點偏差Δx=0.10m、Δy=0.20m、Δz=0.05m，距離e=√(Δx²+Δy²+Δz²)=0.2291m；不是姿態誤差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume reference-point offsets0.10m,0.20m and0.05m. Distance e=√(Δx²+Δy²+Δz²)=0.2291m does not describe orientation error. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用獨立控制點檢查坐標轉換，將吊具參考點換算到構件指定點，另記姿態與接觸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check coordinate transformations against independent control, transfer the rig reference to the specified unit point and record orientation and contact separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設參考點偏差Δx=0.10m、Δy=0.20m、Δz=0.05m，距離e=√(Δx²+Δy²+Δz²)=0.2291m；不是姿態誤差。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume reference-point offsets0.10m,0.20m and0.05m. Distance e=√(Δx²+Δy²+Δz²)=0.2291m does not describe orientation error.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「三維位置與姿態」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Three-dimensional placement geometry\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。","整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches.","Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b284-v15-31","title":"三維位置與姿態：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Three-dimensional placement geometry: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「三維位置與姿態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Three-dimensional placement geometry” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用獨立控制點檢查坐標轉換，將吊具參考點換算到構件指定點，另記姿態與接觸。比較安放前後的水下影像或測量資料，保留量測不確定度與盲區。同時保存三個方向的原始偏差值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check coordinate transformations against independent control, transfer the rig reference to the specified unit point and record orientation and contact separately. Compare underwater observations before and after placement, retaining uncertainty and blind zones. Preserve the original offsets in all three directions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用獨立控制點檢查坐標轉換，將吊具參考點換算到構件指定點，另記姿態與接觸。比較安放前後的水下影像或測量資料，保留量測不確定度與盲區。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check coordinate transformations against independent control, transfer the rig reference to the specified unit point and record orientation and contact separately. Compare underwater observations before and after placement, retaining uncertainty and blind zones.","failure":"注意干擾：參考點選錯可能讓所有坐標一致偏移，姿態未記錄則無法辨識接觸臂翻轉。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An incorrect reference point shifts every coordinate consistently, while missing orientation hides reversed contact arms. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用獨立控制點檢查坐標轉換，將吊具參考點換算到構件指定點，另記姿態與接觸。比較安放前後的水下影像或測量資料，保留量測不確定度與盲區。同時保存三個方向的原始偏差值。","textEn":"Check coordinate transformations against independent control, transfer the rig reference to the specified unit point and record orientation and contact separately. Compare underwater observations before and after placement, retaining uncertainty and blind zones. Preserve the original offsets in all three directions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用獨立控制點檢查坐標轉換，將吊具參考點換算到構件指定點，另記姿態與接觸。比較安放前後的水下影像或測量資料，保留量測不確定度與盲區。","textEn":"Check coordinate transformations against independent control, transfer the rig reference to the specified unit point and record orientation and contact separately. Compare underwater observations before and after placement, retaining uncertainty and blind zones.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「三維位置與姿態」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Three-dimensional placement geometry\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用獨立控制點檢查坐標轉換，將吊具參考點換算到構件指定點，另記姿態與接觸。","抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check coordinate transformations against independent control, transfer the rig reference to the specified unit point and record orientation and contact separately.","Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用獨立控制點檢查坐標轉換，將吊具參考點換算到構件指定點，另記姿態與接觸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check coordinate transformations against independent control, transfer the rig reference to the specified unit point and record orientation and contact separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b284-v15-32","title":"三維位置與姿態：失效診斷","titleEn":"Three-dimensional placement geometry: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「三維位置與姿態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Three-dimensional placement geometry” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"參考點選錯可能讓所有坐標一致偏移，姿態未記錄則無法辨識接觸臂翻轉。點位殘差小仍可能對應水工模型從未驗證過的安放方式，影響後續穩定判讀。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An incorrect reference point shifts every coordinate consistently, while missing orientation hides reversed contact arms. Small position residuals can therefore coexist with an arrangement never validated in the hydraulic model used for stability assessment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：位置距離是三維向量的長度，不會保留偏移方向，方向仍需另行記錄。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Position distance is the magnitude of a three-dimensional vector and does not preserve direction, which must therefore remain separately recorded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「構件參考點位置正確就能證明其朝向與接觸也正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Correct reference-point coordinates prove correct orientation and contacts.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"參考點選錯可能讓所有坐標一致偏移，姿態未記錄則無法辨識接觸臂翻轉。點位殘差小仍可能對應水工模型從未驗證過的安放方式，影響後續穩定判讀。","textEn":"An incorrect reference point shifts every coordinate consistently, while missing orientation hides reversed contact arms. Small position residuals can therefore coexist with an arrangement never validated in the hydraulic model used for stability assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「三維位置與姿態」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Three-dimensional placement geometry\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。","參考點選錯可能讓所有坐標一致偏移，姿態未記錄則無法辨識接觸臂翻轉。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold.","An incorrect reference point shifts every coordinate consistently, while missing orientation hides reversed contact arms."],"answer":2,"explanation":"參考點選錯可能讓所有坐標一致偏移，姿態未記錄則無法辨識接觸臂翻轉。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An incorrect reference point shifts every coordinate consistently, while missing orientation hides reversed contact arms. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b284-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「模型質量縮尺」與「磨耗試驗與壽命」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Model mass scaling\" and \"Abrasion testing and service life\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b284-v15-33","title":"模型質量縮尺：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Model mass scaling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「模型質量縮尺」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Model mass scaling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"幾何縮尺構件的體積按長度三次方變化，相同材料密度才可直接使用相同質量比。實體試驗還需維持相對密度、表面粗糙和接觸方式，不能只做外形相似卻讓有效重量與摩擦特性失去對應。 假設原型質量3000kg、長度比20且材料密度相同，模型質量3000/20³=0.375kg；同時需檢查水下相對密度。 模型接觸面若相對粗糙過大，摩擦行為可能與原型不同，即使質量縮尺正確。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「模型質量縮尺」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Geometrically scaled units change volume with the cube of length, and equal material density permits the same mass ratio. Physical tests also require appropriate relative density, roughness and contacts; matching the silhouette alone does not preserve submerged weight or interface behavior. Assume prototype mass3000kg, length ratio20 and equal material density. Model mass=3000/20³=0.375kg, with submerged relative density checked separately. Excessive relative roughness at model contacts can alter friction even when the mass scaling is correct for the chosen geometry. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Model mass scaling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「模型質量縮尺」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Model mass scaling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-33-k1","title":"模型質量縮尺","titleEn":"Model mass scaling","text":"幾何縮尺構件的體積按長度三次方變化，相同材料密度才可直接使用相同質量比。實體試驗還需維持相對密度、表面粗糙和接觸方式，不能只做外形相似卻讓有效重量與摩擦特性失去對應。","textEn":"Geometrically scaled units change volume with the cube of length, and equal material density permits the same mass ratio. Physical tests also require appropriate relative density, roughness and contacts; matching the silhouette alone does not preserve submerged weight or interface behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模型質量縮尺」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Model mass scaling\" is correct?","options":["幾何縮尺構件的體積按長度三次方變化，相同材料密度才可直接使用相同質量比。","外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。","一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Geometrically scaled units change volume with the cube of length, and equal material density permits the same mass ratio.","Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold.","Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何縮尺構件的體積按長度三次方變化，相同材料密度才可直接使用相同質量比。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Geometrically scaled units change volume with the cube of length, and equal material density permits the same mass ratio. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b284-v15-34","title":"模型質量縮尺：定量估算","titleEn":"Model mass scaling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模型質量縮尺」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Model mass scaling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設原型質量3000kg、長度比20且材料密度相同，模型質量3000/20³=0.375kg；同時需檢查水下相對密度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume prototype mass3000kg, length ratio20 and equal material density. Model mass=3000/20³=0.375kg, with submerged relative density checked separately. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時量模型尺寸、質量及使用水體密度，檢查相對密度和有效重量是否符合試驗設計。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure model dimensions, mass and water density together, verifying relative density and submerged weight against the test design.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設原型質量3000kg、長度比20且材料密度相同，模型質量3000/20³=0.375kg；同時需檢查水下相對密度。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume prototype mass3000kg, length ratio20 and equal material density. Model mass=3000/20³=0.375kg, with submerged relative density checked separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模型質量縮尺」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Model mass scaling\", which statement holds?","options":["每批水表加入相同水量就代表有效水膠比保持不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","完全約束彈性熱應力就是實際混凝土最後一定保留的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Identical metered water addition guarantees an unchanged effective water-to-binder ratio.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Fully restrained elastic thermal stress is the stress the concrete must retain permanently."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b284-v15-35","title":"模型質量縮尺：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Model mass scaling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模型質量縮尺」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Model mass scaling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時量模型尺寸、質量及使用水體密度，檢查相對密度和有效重量是否符合試驗設計。另以安放照片比對接觸點，說明粗糙尺度不能完全相似的限制。檢查模型接觸面的粗糙與摩擦假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure model dimensions, mass and water density together, verifying relative density and submerged weight against the test design. Compare contact points through placement images and state limitations where surface roughness cannot be fully scaled. Check assumptions for model contact roughness and friction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：同時量模型尺寸、質量及使用水體密度，檢查相對密度和有效重量是否符合試驗設計。另以安放照片比對接觸點，說明粗糙尺度不能完全相似的限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure model dimensions, mass and water density together, verifying relative density and submerged weight against the test design. Compare contact points through placement images and state limitations where surface roughness cannot be fully scaled.","failure":"注意干擾：用低密度列印件卻只按長度縮小，模型可能比原型容易移動；額外加重若集中在一點又會改變重心。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Low-density printed units scaled only by length can move more readily than the prototype. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時量模型尺寸、質量及使用水體密度，檢查相對密度和有效重量是否符合試驗設計。另以安放照片比對接觸點，說明粗糙尺度不能完全相似的限制。檢查模型接觸面的粗糙與摩擦假設。","textEn":"Measure model dimensions, mass and water density together, verifying relative density and submerged weight against the test design. Compare contact points through placement images and state limitations where surface roughness cannot be fully scaled. Check assumptions for model contact roughness and friction.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"同時量模型尺寸、質量及使用水體密度，檢查相對密度和有效重量是否符合試驗設計。另以安放照片比對接觸點，說明粗糙尺度不能完全相似的限制。","textEn":"Measure model dimensions, mass and water density together, verifying relative density and submerged weight against the test design. Compare contact points through placement images and state limitations where surface roughness cannot be fully scaled.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模型質量縮尺」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Model mass scaling\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","對稱吊索的理想靜力數值已包含海上起伏造成的動載。","同時量模型尺寸、質量及使用水體密度，檢查相對密度和有效重量是否符合試驗設計。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Ideal symmetric sling forces already include dynamic loading from offshore motion.","Measure model dimensions, mass and water density together, verifying relative density and submerged weight against the test design."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同時量模型尺寸、質量及使用水體密度，檢查相對密度和有效重量是否符合試驗設計。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure model dimensions, mass and water density together, verifying relative density and submerged weight against the test design. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b284-v15-36","title":"模型質量縮尺：失效診斷","titleEn":"Model mass scaling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模型質量縮尺」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Model mass scaling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用低密度列印件卻只按長度縮小，模型可能比原型容易移動；額外加重若集中在一點又會改變重心。質量吻合仍不足以證明動態轉動完全相似。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Low-density printed units scaled only by length can move more readily than the prototype. Concentrated added weight changes gravity center, so even a matching total mass does not establish dynamically similar rotation of the unit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：模型接觸面若相對粗糙過大，摩擦行為可能與原型不同，即使質量縮尺正確。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Excessive relative roughness at model contacts can alter friction even when the mass scaling is correct for the chosen geometry.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外形縮小二十倍時質量也只要縮小二十倍即可。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Scaling the shape down by twenty requires mass to decrease only twentyfold.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用低密度列印件卻只按長度縮小，模型可能比原型容易移動；額外加重若集中在一點又會改變重心。質量吻合仍不足以證明動態轉動完全相似。","textEn":"Low-density printed units scaled only by length can move more readily than the prototype. Concentrated added weight changes gravity center, so even a matching total mass does not establish dynamically similar rotation of the unit.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模型質量縮尺」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Model mass scaling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用低密度列印件卻只按長度縮小，模型可能比原型容易移動；額外加重若集中在一點又會改變重心。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Low-density printed units scaled only by length can move more readily than the prototype.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用低密度列印件卻只按長度縮小，模型可能比原型容易移動；額外加重若集中在一點又會改變重心。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Low-density printed units scaled only by length can move more readily than the prototype. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b284-v15-37","title":"磨耗試驗與壽命：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Abrasion testing and service life: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「磨耗試驗與壽命」如何影響消波塊製作與安放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Abrasion testing and service life” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Wave-dissipating concrete-unit casting and placement”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"表面磨耗可能改變邊角和接觸粗糙度，試驗質量損失提供材料比較，卻不是直接的年損耗率。試驗介質、撞擊能量和時間與現地不同，必須把可重現的試驗排序與實際耐久機制分開。 假設試樣乾質量1.000kg，指定磨耗試驗後0.950kg，損失(1−0.95)/1=5%；不能直接推成每年損失5%。 耐久判讀還需要考慮鹽害與濕乾循環，機械磨耗不是唯一材料退化途徑。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「磨耗試驗與壽命」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Abrasion can alter corners and contact roughness. Test mass loss compares material response but is not a direct annual wear rate. Media, impact energy and duration differ from service, so reproducible laboratory ranking must remain separate from the mechanisms governing real durability. Assume dry sample1.000kg and0.950kg after a specified abrasion test. Loss is5%, which cannot be interpreted as5% annual service loss. Durability interpretation must also consider salt exposure and wet-dry cycling, because mechanical abrasion is not the sole material deterioration mechanism. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Abrasion testing and service life” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「磨耗試驗與壽命」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Abrasion testing and service life”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-37-k1","title":"磨耗試驗與壽命","titleEn":"Abrasion testing and service life","text":"表面磨耗可能改變邊角和接觸粗糙度，試驗質量損失提供材料比較，卻不是直接的年損耗率。試驗介質、撞擊能量和時間與現地不同，必須把可重現的試驗排序與實際耐久機制分開。","textEn":"Abrasion can alter corners and contact roughness. Test mass loss compares material response but is not a direct annual wear rate.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「磨耗試驗與壽命」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Abrasion testing and service life\" is correct?","options":["一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。","表面磨耗可能改變邊角和接觸粗糙度，試驗質量損失提供材料比較，卻不是直接的年損耗率。","任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage.","Abrasion can alter corners and contact roughness.","Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面磨耗可能改變邊角和接觸粗糙度，試驗質量損失提供材料比較，卻不是直接的年損耗率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Abrasion can alter corners and contact roughness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b284-v15-38","title":"磨耗試驗與壽命：定量估算","titleEn":"Abrasion testing and service life: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「磨耗試驗與壽命」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Abrasion testing and service life” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設試樣乾質量1.000kg，指定磨耗試驗後0.950kg，損失(1−0.95)/1=5%；不能直接推成每年損失5%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume dry sample1.000kg and0.950kg after a specified abrasion test. Loss is5%, which cannot be interpreted as5% annual service loss. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對試驗程序、含水條件與秤重時間，記錄失重之外的裂縫和缺角形態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify test procedure, moisture condition and weighing time and record cracking or corner loss beyond mass change.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設試樣乾質量1.000kg，指定磨耗試驗後0.950kg，損失(1−0.95)/1=5%；不能直接推成每年損失5%。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume dry sample1.000kg and0.950kg after a specified abrasion test. Loss is5%, which cannot be interpreted as5% annual service loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「磨耗試驗與壽命」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Abrasion testing and service life\", which statement holds?","options":["整體長度變化很小就表示混凝土內部沒有熱應力。","抗壓試體合格即可證明消波構件吊點和細臂承載都合格。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Small overall length change proves there is no internal thermal stress.","Passing compression specimens also proves adequate lifting points and slender arms.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b284-v15-39","title":"磨耗試驗與壽命：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Abrasion testing and service life: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「磨耗試驗與壽命」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Abrasion testing and service life” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對試驗程序、含水條件與秤重時間，記錄失重之外的裂縫和缺角形態。將不同批次依同方法比較，另以現地追蹤建立環境與材料反應的關聯。確認兩次秤重使用相同乾燥基準。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify test procedure, moisture condition and weighing time and record cracking or corner loss beyond mass change. Compare batches under the same method, using field follow-up separately to relate environment and material response. Confirm identical drying reference conditions for both weighings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對試驗程序、含水條件與秤重時間，記錄失重之外的裂縫和缺角形態。將不同批次依同方法比較，另以現地追蹤建立環境與材料反應的關聯。","observationEn":"Site practice: Verify test procedure, moisture condition and weighing time and record cracking or corner loss beyond mass change. Compare batches under the same method, using field follow-up separately to relate environment and material response.","failure":"注意干擾：試樣表面殘水會掩蓋實際失重，破碎與均勻磨耗又可能有相同總質量差；若據此直接預測剩餘年限，會忽略局部接觸臂受損對結構功能的放大作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Residual water hides actual mass loss, while fragmentation and uniform wear can produce equal changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對試驗程序、含水條件與秤重時間，記錄失重之外的裂縫和缺角形態。將不同批次依同方法比較，另以現地追蹤建立環境與材料反應的關聯。確認兩次秤重使用相同乾燥基準。","textEn":"Verify test procedure, moisture condition and weighing time and record cracking or corner loss beyond mass change. Compare batches under the same method, using field follow-up separately to relate environment and material response. Confirm identical drying reference conditions for both weighings.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對試驗程序、含水條件與秤重時間，記錄失重之外的裂縫和缺角形態。將不同批次依同方法比較，另以現地追蹤建立環境與材料反應的關聯。","textEn":"Verify test procedure, moisture condition and weighing time and record cracking or corner loss beyond mass change. Compare batches under the same method, using field follow-up separately to relate environment and material response.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「磨耗試驗與壽命」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Abrasion testing and service life\"?","options":["核對試驗程序、含水條件與秤重時間，記錄失重之外的裂縫和缺角形態。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","總安放件數達標就能證明每一個區域都有足夠互鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Verify test procedure, moisture condition and weighing time and record cracking or corner loss beyond mass change.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Meeting the total unit count proves adequate interlocking in every local area."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對試驗程序、含水條件與秤重時間，記錄失重之外的裂縫和缺角形態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify test procedure, moisture condition and weighing time and record cracking or corner loss beyond mass change. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b284-v15-40","title":"磨耗試驗與壽命：失效診斷","titleEn":"Abrasion testing and service life: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"prerequisiteIds":["b284-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「磨耗試驗與壽命」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Abrasion testing and service life” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"試樣表面殘水會掩蓋實際失重，破碎與均勻磨耗又可能有相同總質量差；若據此直接預測剩餘年限，會忽略局部接觸臂受損對結構功能的放大作用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Residual water hides actual mass loss, while fragmentation and uniform wear can produce equal changes. Direct lifetime extrapolation then misses how localized damage to a contact arm disproportionately affects the function of the complete unit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：耐久判讀還需要考慮鹽害與濕乾循環，機械磨耗不是唯一材料退化途徑。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Durability interpretation must also consider salt exposure and wet-dry cycling, because mechanical abrasion is not the sole material deterioration mechanism.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「一次磨耗試驗失重百分比就是構件每年的耗損百分比。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mass-loss percentage in one abrasion test equals the unit's annual loss percentage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b284-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"試樣表面殘水會掩蓋實際失重，破碎與均勻磨耗又可能有相同總質量差；若據此直接預測剩餘年限，會忽略局部接觸臂受損對結構功能的放大作用。","textEn":"Residual water hides actual mass loss, while fragmentation and uniform wear can produce equal changes. Direct lifetime extrapolation then misses how localized damage to a contact arm disproportionately affects the function of the complete unit.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]},{"id":"b284-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「磨耗試驗與壽命」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Abrasion testing and service life\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","試樣表面殘水會掩蓋實際失重，破碎與均勻磨耗又可能有相同總質量差；若據此直接預測剩餘年限，會忽略局部接觸臂受損對結構功能的放大作用。","任何形狀的消波塊只要質量相同就有相同水工穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Residual water hides actual mass loss, while fragmentation and uniform wear can produce equal changes.","Concrete armour units of any shape have identical hydraulic stability when mass matches."],"answer":1,"explanation":"試樣表面殘水會掩蓋實際失重，破碎與均勻磨耗又可能有相同總質量差；若據此直接預測剩餘年限，會忽略局部接觸臂受損對結構功能的放大作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Residual water hides actual mass loss, while fragmentation and uniform wear can produce equal changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-afsluitdijk","v15s-eurotop","v15s-cem","v15s-tuas"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
